---
import Concept from '../../layouts/Concept.astro';
import { siteUrl } from '../../utils/site';
import plans from '../../data/weapon-adaptation-tasks.json';
---
<Concept title="All-weapon adaptation plan and test protocol" section="States">
<p><strong>Pair-by-pair implementation in progress.</strong> The approved HUmar/saber fixture is the reference, not proof of all-weapon readiness. Each adaptation below is independently tracked by ID and gender. Start with shared foundations, then enable profiles only after their own acceptance gate. A missing source mapping is a blocker for that role, not a reason to silently borrow another weapon.</p>
<p><a href={siteUrl('/states/weapon-animation-mappings/')}>Mapping inventory</a> · <a href={siteUrl('/states/weapon-state-transitions/')}>UML transitions</a> · <a href="https://github.com/kion-dgl/psz-godot/pull/791">Persistent checklist on PR #791</a></p>
<h2>Shared work before adapting profiles</h2>
<table><thead><tr><th>ID</th><th>Work</th><th>Exit gate</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>P00</td><td>Checkpoint approved prototype and exact assets. Keep class/fixture restrictions while generalization is incomplete.</td><td>Recoverable commit, matching asset hashes, documented setup and known failures.</td></tr>
<tr><td>P01</td><td>Audit all source/gender/role mappings; record missing clips and class overrides. Build an inspection fixture with explicit weapon, avatar and role selection.</td><td>Every cell resolves to a verified clip or approved fallback; no hidden suffix-based selection.</td></tr>
<tr><td>P02</td><td>Extract shared logical states and a typed weapon-animation/timing profile. Separate animation roles from enum values and contact delivery.</td><td>Saber behavior unchanged; normal/strong share continuation windows; failed/stopped/completed outcomes distinct; profile swap clears pending state.</td></tr>
<tr><td>P03</td><td>Generalize hit delivery: single/multi-hit melee, bursts, thrown projectiles, explosions and beams. Resolve accuracy/evasion, guard and flinch policy beyond the fixture.</td><td>Preserve hit counts, target caps, immunity and enemy-specific reactions. No artificial accuracy override or guaranteed guard quietly becomes campaign policy.</td></tr>
<tr><td>P04</td><td>Publish reproducible animation/audio assets and update pack/sidecar metadata. Include source WAV or a pre-softened imported cue for click-free playback.</td><td>Clean checkout and exported build reproduce clips and sounds without this machine's ignored files.</td></tr>
<tr><td>P05</td><td>Run per-profile tests, cross-weapon regression, campaign routes, bosses and export checks. Enable only approved profiles.</td><td>Owner checklist complete for enabled profiles, outstanding failures classified, rollback gate retained until rollout approved.</td></tr>
</tbody></table>
<h2>Plan for each adaptation</h2>
<p>M and F are separate test rows. A shared profile may reuse a clip only when that reuse is explicit and visually checked. Core human, CAST and proportion variants need coverage; gender alone does not certify every avatar.</p>
{plans.map(plan => <details id={plan.id.toLowerCase()}><summary>{plan.id} — {plan.name}</summary><p><strong>{plan.status}</strong><br/>Dependencies: {plan.depends}<br/>{plan.scope}</p><ol>{plan.steps.map(step => <li>{step}</li>)}</ol><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> {plan.acceptance}</p><p>Record results as <code>{plan.id}-M</code> and <code>{plan.id}-F</code>; apply W01–W10 below plus the family-specific acceptance checks.</p></details>)}
<h2>Per-profile test checklist</h2>
<p>Run each test on the actual selected avatar, weapon and asset pack. A checkbox means the entire row passed at the recorded revision, not merely that the animations loaded. Record partial progress by test ID before leaving.</p>
<table><thead><tr><th>ID</th><th>Test and expected result</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>W01</td><td>Inspect every role in the mapping table: correct gender/class source, posture, grip, foot planting, root alignment, blend, dodge and defeated/get-up fallbacks. Record omitted roles explicitly.</td></tr>
<tr><td>W02</td><td>Idle stays relaxed. Approach before cursor acquisition does not trigger caution. Cursor engages caution; retreat keeps it for 500 ms then runs. Reacquisition resets the countdown.</td></tr>
<tr><td>W03</td><td>First normal/strong attack has readable ready preparation and blends. Test every N/S pattern for the actual step count (three steps: NNN, NNS, NSN, NSS, SNN, SNS, SSN, SSS). Same continuation window for both attack types.</td></tr>
<tr><td>W04</td><td>Press too early and too late: finish swing, then stationary exposed recovery. Withhold input: movement returns before attack cooldown ends. Complete sequence: ready stance and eligible frontal guard before movement returns.</td></tr>
<tr><td>W05</td><td>Verify every contact/release timestamp, hit count, target cap and geometry. Test near/far targets, rear targets and moving enemies. Projectiles produce impact feedback only on actual damage; no duplicate release.</td></tr>
<tr><td>W06</td><td>Strong charge cue/small weapon particles; subtle normal impact; stronger impact/flinch only on accepted damage. No ground rings or whole-body glow; no noisy multi-hit feedback or permanent stagger.</td></tr>
<tr><td>W07</td><td>Palette circles match real acceptance timing; no cue for nonexistent next step. Lock cursor sounds on acquisition/change, stays silent while held or briefly flickering, and has no audible click.</td></tr>
<tr><td>W08</td><td>Interrupt preparation, swing and recovery with damage/knockdown; exercise block, rear hits, status ticks, freeze, dodge, defeat and revival. No stale action resumes; immunity and boss exceptions survive.</td></tr>
<tr><td>W09</td><td>Swap/equip/unequip weapon, change palette, cast techniques, open/close menus, transition areas and return to city. No old profile timers, queued shot or lingering effects.</td></tr>
<tr><td>W10</td><td>Repeat against solo/group enemies and one appropriate boss; verify keyboard/controller and an exported build. Record commit, pack hash, avatar, weapon, scenario, result and evidence.</td></tr>
</tbody></table>
<h2>AFK / resume protocol</h2>
<ol><li>Use the PR description as the persistent checklist. Record the commit and asset-pack SHA before starting; local uncommitted changes must be identified separately.</li><li>Choose one profile/gender row. Record the avatar/class, actual weapon ID, solo/group/boss scenario and the next W-test.</li><li>On failure, leave the row unchecked and record the test ID, expected/actual result, reproduction input and screenshot/log. Do not block unrelated profile tests unless the failure is shared.</li><li>Before AFK, update “Resume here” on the PR with the next exact test. Restarting the current fixture resets the encounter; campaign saves are isolated.</li><li>After a code or asset change, mark affected completed rows for retest. A prior owner approval of the saber feel is not all-weapon or clean-export approval.</li></ol>
<p>The current launcher supports HUmar and HUmarl saber through <code>--gender male|female</code>, <code>--group</code>, <code>--check</code> and <code>--rendered</code>. Other profile rows remain blocked on P01/P02 and their adaptation; <code>--weapon sword</code> selects Sword for either gender. Both saber and sword pairs are owner-approved. <code>--weapon daggers</code> selects Daggers for either gender. Both dagger pairs are owner-approved. <code>--weapon claw</code> supports both genders. Both Claw pairs are owner-approved. <code>--weapon double-saber</code> supports both genders; both owner-approved. <code>--weapon spear</code> supports both genders with explicit shared PSO partisan donors; both owner-approved. <code>--weapon slicer</code> supports male; owner playtest pending. Exact current setup and launch commands are in <code>docs/weapon-adaptation-plan.md</code> and the PR.</p>
</Concept>
